  "content": {
    "title": "UFC 327 live updates: Carlos Ulberg stops Jiri Prochazka in stunner",
    "text": "Live from Miami, UFC 327 is live with one of the biggest cards of the year. We’re here at Kaseya Center, where 12 fights are expected to energize a wild crowd on Saturday night. The card begins at 5 p.m. ET, with prelims and the main card at 9 p.m. ET, with a two-hour window on CBS before going over to Paramount+. President Donald Trump is expected to attend tonight’s event, adding another interesting bit of intrigue to this already scintillating card. Follow The Post for the latest UFC 327 updates, news, and more. That's a wrap at UFC 327 By erichternyp and Erich Richter Phenomenal card where a new star was born and a champion was crowned. Carlos Ulberg win isn't the best result for the UFCBy erichternyp and Erich Richter Honestly, this is a nightmare for the UFC, as light heavyweight will be in a full standstill for the next year. Ulberg is looking likely to be forced into medical scans and a lengthy recovery process, assuming the injury is what we think it is. For Prochazka, Ulberg's injury could get him an interim shot at the light heavyweight belt. Carlos Ulberg says he has mixed emotions following winBy erichternyp and Erich Richter Perhaps the saddest post-fight press conference you will see from a winner. Carlos Ulberg said, \"Hopefully it's not as bad as it may seem.\" He is headed for scans of his leg and added that it's hard to really celebrate this win. Paulo Costa also injured in winBy Erich Richter Paulo Costa had to be wheeled into the press conference post-fight and said he injured his leg from kicking his opponent so much. He adds that he believes he is close to a title fight at light heavyweight despite this being his first fight in the division. Dana White says that Carlos Ulberg tore his ACLBy Erich Richter At the post-fight press conference, Dana White said that it believed that Ulberg tore his ACL. He will be out indefinitely, perhaps until 2027. Jiri Prochazka stopped by Carlos UlbergBy Erich Richter What a disaster for Jiri Prochazka. Ulberg clearly injured his leg and Prochazka let up from kicking his leg to score a win. The result is Ulberg getting time to recover and then knocking Prochazka out moments later. A new light heavyweight champion. Josh Hokit vs. Derrick Lewis added to White House cardBy Erich Richter A true stunner, that's how big he just got after his win vs. Curtis Blaydes. Costa looks as good as ever against Azamat Murzakanov Costa was a big underdog coming into this fight and he is really putting it on Murzakanov during round three. Kicks and punches are all working. And there it is, head kick TKO from Costa, Murzakanov was exhausted in there. Costa looks excellent. Winning the fight so far midway through two.By erichternyp and Erich Richter Perfect start for Costa, who is forcing Murzakanov to chase him around the octagon. Costa looks in shape, good cardio, and kicks ot the body. It's rare to find a fighter that is this comfortable fighting with his back to the cage, but Costa doesn't feel trapped at all in there. Timid start between Paulo Costa and Azamat MurzakanovBy Erich Richter Costa on his back foot the whole time, but I think he wants it that way. Murzakanov is having a tough time catching up right now. Costa landed a right hand, and it looked to hurt Murzakanov. Costa pointed at him to let him know he saw that he was hurt. Good kicks from Costa, he looks phenomenal. 10-9 Costa after round one. Paulo Costa vs. Azamat Murzakanov coming up nextBy Erich RichterWill be impossible to follow that Hokit-Blaydes fight. Best fight we've seen in a long time. Fight of the year so far for sure. Blaydes' face looks beat up after losing to Josh HokitBy erichternyp and Erich Richter",
